  "note": "Four print columns -- name, role, name, role -- at offsets ~29, ~65, ~101 and ~136-143; read as two name/role pairs split at offset 95. Line 2 carries the column headers 'Role' over each role column along with the two section headings, and is filed under headings. On line 40 the left role column overruns and collides with the right name column, printing 'para/substitute admin asst. Roger Hanks' as one run; it is split back into the left-hand entry 'Alicia McAllister / para/substitute admin asst.' and the right-hand entry 'Roger Hanks / Custodian/Night'. The heading on line 32 is printed 'Paraprofessionals_' with a trailing underscore, which is how an underline came through extraction; it is kept verbatim in grade_or_dept. Likewise 'Gr: 5 Para' on line 39 is printed with a colon where the other rows print a full stop, and 'café' in lower case on lines 33-34; both are left as printed."
